 Re-running `connect` keeps the stable installation identity, rotates device authorization, refreshes
 the installed connector copy, and updates only Vibe Racing-owned hooks. Hook reconciliation is
 best-effort per source: one damaged settings file is reported without blocking healthy hooks or the
-initial sync. The final token/config swap is serialized behind any active sync, so an older request
+initial sync. If the server reports that the previous authorization is revoked (401 or 403),
+`connect` removes the stale local authorization and automatic state through the normal lifecycle
+cleanup, then starts a fresh pairing without requiring `disconnect`; the installation identity and
+local source definitions remain stable. Other reconciliation errors retain the previous connection.
+Incomplete auxiliary cleanup is reported as a warning, while the revoked authorization is still
+removed. The final token/config swap is serialized behind any active sync, so an older request
 cannot restore superseded authorization.
 
